{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:1.1-5", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-5"}, "paraphrase": "Ṛbhu performs austerity for twelve divine years; the Lord appears as Varāha and offers a boon; Ṛbhu asks for the knowledge that frees from saṃsāra.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:rbhu", "tch:varaha"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:1.16-17", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.16-17"}, "paraphrase": "Worshippers of Varāha become liberated while living; those who know the ninety-six are freed in any stage of life, whether matted, shaven or with topknot.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:1.6-15", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.6-15"}, "paraphrase": "The principles are counted as 24, 36 or 96; the ninety-six add to the 24 the five elements, three bodies, three states, six modifications, six waves (hunger, thirst, grief, delusion, old age, death), six sheaths, six enemies, three jīvas, three guṇas, three karmas, five actions, four inner functions, the four sublime attitudes (friendliness, compassion, joy, equanimity) and fourteen deities.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:ninety-six-tattvas"], "obstacles": ["obs:six-urmis", "obs:six-enemies"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:2.1-6", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.1-6"}, "paraphrase": "The fourfold means (discrimination, dispassion, the six virtues, desire for liberation) come by one's dharma of caste and stage, austerity and pleasing the guru.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadhana-catustaya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:2.39-40", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.39-40"}, "paraphrase": "True fasting (upavāsa) is 'dwelling near' — the jīva abiding with the supreme Self — not drying up the body; beating the anthill does not kill the snake.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:2.41-42", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.41-42"}, "paraphrase": "'Brahman is' is indirect knowledge; 'I am Brahman' is direct; the knower is liberated while living from the moment of knowing.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:2.76", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.76"}, "paraphrase": "Renouncing objects, seeing the truth, and the natural state are hard to gain without the grace of a true guru.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:2.78-79-summary", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.78-79 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "An analogy between mercury and mind (both are fixed by the right means) is given; no procedure for mercury is recorded here.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:2.80", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.80"}, "paraphrase": "Mind is lord of the senses, breath lord of the mind, and dissolution (laya) lord of the breath.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "body-layers"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:3.26-30", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3.26-30"}, "paraphrase": "The ignorant seek powers through substances, mantras, rites and times; the knower does not, for powers do not lead to the supreme.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "dispute"], "obstacles": ["obs:siddhis-as-obstacles"], "disputes": ["dsp:siddhis-sign-or-obstacle"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:4.1-10", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.1-10"}, "paraphrase": "Nidāgha asks about the stages; Ṛbhu teaches seven: good desire (śubhecchā), inquiry (vicāraṇā), thinning of mind (tanumānasī), attainment of sattva (sattvāpatti), non-attachment (asaṃsakti), non-perception of objects (padārthabhāvanā) and the fourth (turyagā); each is defined.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:seven-bhumikas"], "paths": ["pth:varaha-seven-bhumikas"], "teachers": ["tch:rbhu", "tch:nidagha"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:4.11-16", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.11-16"}, "paraphrase": "In the first three stages the world is seen as in waking, in the fourth as in dream, in the fifth as in deep sleep; the sixth is like sleepiness within that; the seventh is deep sleep of the world entirely.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:seven-bhumikas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:4.2-3-pranava-mapping", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.2-3 (praṇava mapping)"}, "paraphrase": "The stages are mapped onto the measures of Oṃ (a, u, m, half-measure, each gross, subtle, seed and witness); the first three are the seeker's, the fourth makes a knower of Brahman, the fifth the excellent, the sixth the more excellent, the seventh the most excellent knower.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:seven-bhumikas", "cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:4.21-30", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.21-30"}, "paraphrase": "Marks of the one liberated in life: free of 'I' and 'mine', equal-minded, untouched by the body's experiences.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:4.34-42", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.34-42"}, "paraphrase": "Two paths: Śuka's path of the bird (vihaṅgama), immediate liberation through inquiry into the great sayings; Vāmadeva's path of the ant (pipīlikā), gradual liberation over births through yoga — a haṭha practitioner hindered by obstacles or powers is reborn in a great family and continues. Both reach Brahman.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:bird-and-ant-paths"], "teachers": ["tch:suka", "tch:vamadeva"], "disputes": ["dsp:sudden-or-gradual"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:5.10", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.10"}, "paraphrase": "Mantra, laya and haṭha yoga suit practitioners of dull, middling and superior capacity.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-yogas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:5.50-55", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.50-55"}, "paraphrase": "The kuṇḍalinī lies in the triangle at the base; she is the supreme power from which breath, fire, bindu, nāda, haṃsa and mind arise; the six centres are the seat of Śakti, from the throat to the crown the seat of Śambhu.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini", "cpt:cakras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:5.58", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.58"}, "paraphrase": "Prāṇāyāma of knowledge: exhalation is the renunciation of all external objects, inhalation the scriptural knowledge, retention one's own realization.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:jnana-pranayama"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:5.64-67", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.64-67"}, "paraphrase": "The three knots are pierced by yoga and by the grace of guru and god, through saṃskāras of many births.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-granthis"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:varaha-upanisad:5.71-75", "source": "src:varaha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.71-75"}, "paraphrase": "Four stages: ārambha (outer rites set aside, inner performed), ghaṭa, paricaya and niṣpatti (natural yoga, liberation while living).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:yogatattva-four-avasthas"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-avasthas-of-yoga"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
